  "lineage": "Mid-fifteenth-century compositional school centered on the courts of the Dukes of Burgundy (Philip the Good, Charles the Bold) at Dijon and Brussels. Guillaume Dufay (c.1397-1474) and Gilles Binchois (c.1400-1460) are the principal composers. Developed the Mass cycle (cyclic Mass based on a single cantus firmus), the rondeau and ballade chanson forms, and the smoother-consonant fauxbourdon harmonic style. Direct precursor of the Franco-Flemish polyphonic school.",
